title: Technical Nutrient
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

An aluminum [[Navy Chair]] can be melted down and made into another chair, and that one into another. Nothing is lost and nothing goes back to the soil.

That is a technical nutrient: a metal, plastic, or other made material that can't safely rot, so it is kept going around inside industry. The term is from [[Cradle to Cradle]], and it is the partner to a [[Biological Nutrient]].

The ways to keep one going, best first: reuse it, repair it, rebuild it, and last of all recycle it.

None of that works unless the thing can be taken apart. Fuse it to something else and you get a [[Monstrous Hybrid]].

See [[Aluminum]], [[Polyethylene]], [[Downcycling]], [[Design for Disassembly]]
